{
  "approved": false,
  "issues": [
    "The evaluator treats event=accept as name confirmation, although Brief A rule 3 explicitly excludes generic assent such as 'go ahead'. The initial prompt also references identity_prompt and callback_facts before either is initialized.",
    "Security-result prompts are overwritten when verify returns through evaluate. The existing phase_after_result flag is never consumed. A complete corrected answer can also be concatenated with an obsolete partial answer, preventing the corrected answer from reaching verification.",
    "After a verification service failure, the hold branch ignores a newly supplied corrected answer and only permits resubmission of the previous answer.",
    "The callback implementation invents a requirement that an invalid proposal must contain both date and time before consuming the retry allowance. Brief A rule 7 applies when either the offered day or time is outside the window. Impossible dates also bypass this allowance indefinitely.",
    "A third party who supplies callback details in their first reply has those details discarded by the third_party branch.",
    "Product extraction requests internal product IDs without supplying those IDs to the extraction model. The schema also cannot represent different amounts or dates for multiple products in one reply, and an aggregate amount can be incorrectly applied separately to every product.",
    "Clarifications discard the proposal being clarified. For example, a read-back correction with an unspecified product loses its date when the customer subsequently identifies the product. A shared vague date becomes a first-product-only proposal, and its associated amount can be lost.",
    "The amount branches discard a simultaneously proposed date when offering the floor or full amount. A repeated below-floor proposal can also consume a persuasion attempt even though a proposed amount is not a refusal.",
    "A hardship statement containing a voluntary date or amount bypasses the required support offer instead of preserving the proposal while offering support.",
    "When an already-paid claim resolves the last product, advance discards the required statement that payments can take one business day to appear.",
    "The confirmation branch routes directly to save_promise without passing through the validation performed by the writing branch.",
    "Every extracted factual question receives 'I do not have that information', including questions answerable from the loaded account."
  ],
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/policy/third_party/invalid_callback_budget",
      "value": "An explicitly supplied day or time outside the allowed window is an invalid proposal even if the other component is missing. Ask once for another proposal; after a second invalid proposal, do not schedule and close not_reached/no_callback. A merely missing or ambiguous component is not itself an invalid proposal."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables",
      "value": {
        "identity_prompt": "",
        "callback_facts": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/task_message",
      "value": "Check conversation history first. If the opening has not been spoken, first say exactly: 'I am a digital assistant calling from Freya Bank, and this call is recorded.' This also applies when chat starts with the caller's first message. Never repeat an opening already spoken. If that first caller message is merely a greeting and no name question precedes it, ask 'Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}?' and wait; do not treat the greeting as an unsuccessful answer to a question not yet asked. Otherwise submit the new substantive reply for evaluation. On entry after evaluation, speak the supplied identity_prompt: {{identity_prompt}}. If no instruction is present, ask the name question. Callback facts: {{callback_facts}}. No bank tool is available here. For each new caller reply, invoke transition_to_evaluate once before advancing; do not resubmit a reply already processed. Only yes, that's me, speaking or the customer's own name confirms identity; 'go ahead' does not. Let the evaluator supply AI/scam answers and the next question rather than answering twice. Relatives cannot supply security answers. Never guess or hint at a security answer. During a service hold, process a newly supplied answer or explicit retry request; disclose no account information."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/extraction_schema/0/description",
      "value": "Classify only the newest caller reply using the question actually asked in history. Overwrite each turn. name_yes requires yes, that's me, speaking or the target customer's own name in response to the name question. Hello, go ahead and who is this are not name_yes or accept at the name stage. accept is reserved for accepting the offer to help first. Security answers, including corrected answers after a failed service operation, are answer even if incomplete. Refusal to answer and asking what the call is about are refuse/about. A relative offering payment is third_party; still extract any callback date and time supplied in that reply. Human requests or insistence are human. A request to repeat an unsuccessful operation without a new answer is retry."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collection/extraction_schema/3/description",
      "value": "Scope stated in the newest reply: all, current, a spoken product label such as credit card ending 4821 or personal loan, or an ordinal such as first product. Preserve an unambiguous actual product_id only if it is present in the available history. Do not invent or guess IDs. Leave empty when unstated or ambiguous. A reply identifying a product after a clarification still populates this field even when it contains no new amount or date."
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collection/extraction_schema/-",
      "value": {
        "name": "proposal_items",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Overwrite each turn. When the newest reply explicitly proposes different terms for multiple products, return a JSON array of objects with scope, amount_text and date_text strings. Use spoken product labels or ordinals for scope, decimal digits for amounts, and preserve relative dates. Omit missing fields rather than inventing terms. Use the final corrected terms. Example syntax only: [{"scope":"first product","amount_text":"100","date_text":"tomorrow"},{"scope":"second product","date_text":"next Friday"}]. Otherwise return an empty string. Do not put an aggregate total into separate product amounts.",
        "min_confidence": 0.6
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collection/extraction_schema/-",
      "value": {
        "name": "amount_scope",
        "type": "string",
        "enum_values": [
          "each",
          "total",
          "unspecified"
        ],
        "description": "Overwrite each turn. each only if the caller explicitly proposes the same amount separately for each product. total if the amount is an aggregate across products. unspecified otherwise. Never infer that an aggregate or unqualified amount applies separately to every product.",
        "min_confidence": 0.6
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collection/task_message",
      "value": "Speak the newly computed collection_prompt faithfully, preserving figures and required questions: {{collection_prompt}}. Verified facts: {{account_facts}}. Current product state: {{ledger_text}}. Account-question mode: {{answer_account_question}}. If that mode is yes, first answer the caller's latest factual question using only the verified facts and conversation history. If those sources do not provide the answer, say 'I do not have that information.' Then repeat only the outstanding question, not the whole debt announcement or previous explanation. No bank tool is available here. On each NEW caller reply, invoke transition_to_evaluate once; do not invoke again merely on entry with an already-processed reply. Let the evaluator validate proposals and select offers before speaking them. Do not add willingness or affordability questions. Never ask how much the customer can pay. Describe all products before the first payment question and do not repeat the today question per product. A date or amount proposal is not a refusal. Hardship takes precedence over ordinary persuasion and restructuring. Historical payoff or closure is a dispute; payment of the current overdue amount is paid. Read all pending promises together and ask 'Do you confirm?'. Changed terms require a new read-back and yes. Recorded promises cannot be changed or cancelled here. Preserve the complete history."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/evaluate/code",
      "value": "try:
    import json, re, datetime
    vars['route'] = 'identity'
    for k in ['identity_prompt', 'collection_prompt', 'closing_speech', 'account_facts', 'callback_facts', 'ledger_text']:
        vars.setdefault(k, '')
    for k, v in [('phase', 'name'), ('verification_state', 'unverified'), ('account_state', 'empty'), ('name_asks', 1), ('wrong_answers', 0), ('identity_refusals', 0), ('talk_refusals', 0), ('human_asked', 'no'), ('close_attempted', 'no'), ('close_state', 'not_called'), ('closing_ready', 'no')]:
        vars.setdefault(k, v)
    vars['answer_account_question'] = 'no'
    holidays = set(['2026-10-26', '2026-11-11', '2026-11-26', '2026-12-25', '2027-01-01'])
    now = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(str(vars.get('now', '')).replace('Z', '+00:00')).replace(tzinfo=None)
    today = now.date()
    def business(d):
        return d.weekday() < 5 and d.isoformat() not in holidays
    def next_business(d):
        while not business(d):
            d += datetime.timedelta(days=1)
        return d
    def after_business(d, n):
        for unused in range(n):
            d = next_business(d + datetime.timedelta(days=1))
        return d
    def week_end(d):
        x = d - datetime.timedelta(days=d.weekday()) + datetime.timedelta(days=4)
        while not business(x):
            x -= datetime.timedelta(days=1)
        return x
    first_day = week_end(today)
    if first_day <= today:
        first_day = week_end(today + datetime.timedelta(days=7))
    vars['first_offer_day'] = first_day.isoformat()
    callback_next = after_business(today, 1)
    vars['callback_facts'] = 'Eligible dates: ' + today.isoformat() + ' or ' + callback_next.isoformat() + '; 10:00 through 19:00 inclusive, strictly after ' + now.isoformat(timespec='minutes') + '.'
    months = dict(january=1, february=2, march=3, april=4, may=5, june=6, july=7, august=8, september=9, october=10, november=11, december=12)
    weekdays = dict(monday=0, tuesday=1, wednesday=2, thursday=3, friday=4, saturday=5, sunday=6)
    def clean(s):
        s = str(s or '').strip().lower()
        parts = re.split(r'\b(?:sorry|i mean|actually)\b|\bno[, :]+', s)
        return parts[-1].strip() if len(parts) > 1 else s
    def parse_day(text, birth=False):
        s = clean(text)
        if not s:
            return '', 'missing'
        if not birth:
            if s == 'today':
                return today.isoformat(), 'exact'
            if s == 'tomorrow':
                return (today + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat(), 'exact'
            if s in ['day after tomorrow', 'the day after tomorrow']:
                return (today + datetime.timedelta(days=2)).isoformat(), 'exact'
            m = re.fullmatch(r'(next|this)\s+(monday|tuesday|wednesday|thursday|friday|saturday|sunday)', s)
            if m:
                base = today - datetime.timedelta(days=today.weekday())
                return (base + datetime.timedelta(days=weekdays[m.group(2)] + (7 if m.group(1) == 'next' else 0))).isoformat(), 'exact'
            if s in weekdays:
                return '', 'ambiguous'
            if any(x in s for x in ['next week', 'end of', 'salary', 'sometime', 'later', 'soon']):
                return '', 'vague'
        try:
            m = re.fullmatch(r'(\d{4})-(\d{1,2})-(\d{1,2})', s)
            if m:
                return datetime.date(int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2)), int(m.group(3))).isoformat(), 'exact'
            nums = re.findall(r'\d+', s)
            month = next((v for k, v in months.items() if re.search(r'\b' + k + r'\b', s)), 0)
            if month:
                if birth and len(nums) > 2 and len(''.join(nums[1:])) == 4 and all(len(x) < 4 for x in nums[1:]):
                    nums = [nums[0], ''.join(nums[1:])]
                years = [x for x in nums if len(x) == 4]
                days = [x for x in nums if len(x) != 4]
                if len(days) != 1 or len(years) > 1 or (birth and len(years) != 1):
                    return '', 'missing'
                year = int(years[0]) if years else today.year
                return datetime.date(year, month, int(days[0])).isoformat(), 'exact'
            if birth and len(nums) > 3 and len(''.join(nums[2:])) == 4:
                nums = nums[:2] + [''.join(nums[2:])]
            if len(nums) == 3 and len(nums[2]) == 4:
                return datetime.date(int(nums[2]), int(nums[1]), int(nums[0])).isoformat(), 'exact'
            return '', 'missing' if len(nums) < 3 else 'ambiguous'
        except Exception:
            return '', 'invalid'
    def number(s):
        t = re.sub(r'[,\s]', '', str(s))
        if not re.fullmatch(r'-?\d+(?:\.\d+)?', t):
            raise ValueError('Incomplete amount')
        return float(t)
    def money(x):
        return str(int(x)) if float(x).is_integer() else str(x)
    def speak_day(s):
        d = datetime.date.fromisoformat(s)
        names = ['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June', 'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December']
        return str(d.day) + ' ' + names[d.month - 1] + ' ' + str(d.year)
    def structured(value, fallback):
        if isinstance(value, str):
            try:
                value = json.loads(value)
            except Exception:
                return fallback
        return value if isinstance(value, type(fallback)) else fallback
    ledger = structured(vars.get('ledger', []), [])
    notes = structured(vars.get('successful_notes', dict()), dict())
    event = str(vars.get('event', '') or 'none')
    phase = str(vars.get('phase', 'name'))
    dt = str(vars.get('date_text', '') or '')
    amount_text = str(vars.get('amount_text', '') or '')
    scope = str(vars.get('product_scope', '') or '')
    amount_scope = str(vars.get('amount_scope', '') or 'unspecified')
    items = structured(vars.get('proposal_items', []), [])
    target_name = (str(vars.get('title', '')) + ' ' + str(vars.get('last_name', ''))).strip()
    name_question = 'Am I speaking with ' + target_name + '?'
    def identity_say(s):
        vars['identity_prompt'] = s
        vars['route'] = 'identity'
    def collection_say(s):
        if vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified' or vars.get('account_state') != 'ready' or not ledger:
            raise ValueError('Account prerequisites missing')
        vars['collection_prompt'] = s
        vars['route'] = 'collection'
    def hold(operation, message):
        vars['failed_operation'] = operation
        vars['hold_message'] = message
        vars['phase'] = 'hold'
        identity_say(message)
    def early_close(outcome, reason, prefix=''):
        vars['close_outcome'] = outcome
        vars['close_reason'] = reason
        vars['final_prefix'] = prefix
        vars['phase'] = 'finalize'
        finalize()
    def request_transfer(queue):
        if notes:
            hold('finalization', 'I am sorry, I cannot complete another action during this final step.')
            return
        if queue != 'general' and (vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified' or vars.get('account_state') != 'ready'):
            raise ValueError('Account transfer prerequisites missing')
        vars['requested_queue'] = queue
        vars['resume_phase'] = phase
        vars['route'] = 'transfer'
    def set_offer(row, amount, day, kind, prefix=''):
        signature = money(amount) + '|' + day
        if signature in row.get('rejected', []) and kind != 'proposal':
            return False
        row['offer_amount'] = amount
        row['offer_date'] = day
        row['offer_kind'] = kind
        row['question'] = prefix + 'Can you pay ' + money(amount) + ' for your ' + row['label'] + ' on ' + speak_day(day) + '?'
        return True
    def persuasion(row):
        if vars.get('hardship_active') == 'yes':
            row['status'] = 'hardship'
            return
        while row['attempts'] < row['budget']:
            row['attempts'] += 1
            amount = row['floor'] if row['attempts'] == 2 or row.get('full_too_much') == 'yes' else row['past_due']
            day = row['deadline'] if row['attempts'] == 2 else first_day.isoformat()
            prefix = 'The rest stays overdue. ' if amount < row['past_due'] else ''
            if set_offer(row, amount, day, 'persuasion', prefix):
                row['status'] = 'open'
                return
        row['status'] = 'refused'
    def advance(prefix=''):
        opened = next((r for r in ledger if r['status'] == 'open'), None)
        if opened:
            vars['phase'] = 'product'
            vars['current_product'] = opened['product_id']
            if not opened.get('question'):
                persuasion(opened)
                if opened['status'] != 'open':
                    advance(prefix)
                    return
            collection_say(prefix + opened['question'])
            return
        agreed = [r for r in ledger if r['status'] == 'agreed']
        if agreed:
            vars['phase'] = 'confirm'
            text = ' '.join('For your ' + r['label'] + ', ' + money(r['offer_amount']) + ' on ' + speak_day(r['offer_date']) + '.' for r in agreed)
            collection_say(prefix + text + ' Do you confirm?')
            return
        if prefix:
            vars['final_prefix'] = (str(vars.get('final_prefix', '')) + ' ' + prefix).strip()
        vars['phase'] = 'finalize'
        finalize()
    def finalize():
        vars['closing_ready'] = 'no'
        outcome = ''
        reason = ''
        if vars.get('transfer_state') == 'succeeded':
            outcome = 'transferred'
            reason = str(vars.get('transfer_reason', ''))
        elif vars.get('close_outcome') in ['not_reached', 'not_verified']:
            outcome = vars['close_outcome']
            reason = str(vars.get('close_reason', ''))
        else:
            if vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified' or vars.get('account_state') != 'ready' or not ledger:
                hold('finalization', 'I am sorry, I cannot complete this right now.')
                return
            allowed = ['recorded', 'refused', 'hardship', 'dispute', 'paid', 'service_error']
            if any(r.get('status') not in allowed for r in ledger):
                hold('finalization', 'I am sorry, I cannot complete this right now.')
                return
            for row in ledger:
                if row['status'] != 'recorded' and notes.get(row['product_id']) != row['status']:
                    vars['pending_note'] = dict(product_id=row['product_id'], reason=row['status'])
                    vars['notes_started'] = 'yes'
                    vars['route'] = 'note'
                    return
            if any(r['status'] == 'recorded' for r in ledger):
                outcome = 'promise'
            elif all(r['status'] == 'paid' for r in ledger):
                outcome = 'paid'
            else:
                outcome = 'no_promise'
                reason = next(r['status'] for r in ledger if r['status'] != 'paid')
        permitted = dict(transferred=['restructuring', 'human', 'support'], no_promise=['refused', 'hardship', 'dispute', 'service_error'], not_verified=['failed', 'declined'], not_reached=['callback', 'no_callback', 'wrong_number', 'deceased', 'unclear'])
        if outcome not in ['promise', 'paid'] and reason not in permitted.get(outcome, []):
            raise ValueError('Unsupported close combination')
        vars['close_outcome'] = outcome
        vars['close_reason'] = reason
        parts = []
        if vars.get('final_prefix'):
            parts.append(str(vars['final_prefix']))
        recorded = [r for r in ledger if r.get('status') == 'recorded']
        if recorded:
            parts.append('I have recorded ' + '; '.join('your promise of ' + money(r['offer_amount']) + ' for your ' + r['label'] + ' on ' + speak_day(r['offer_date']) for r in recorded) + '.')
            parts.append('You will receive a text message confirming this promise.')
        for row in ledger:
            if row.get('status') == 'service_error':
                parts.append('I could not record the promise for your ' + row['label'] + '.')
        if outcome == 'transferred':
            teams = dict(human='a member of our team', support='the customer support team', restructuring='the restructuring team')
            parts.append('I am connecting you with ' + teams[reason] + '.')
        parts.append('Thank you. Goodbye.')
        vars['closing_speech'] = ' '.join(parts)
        vars['closing_ready'] = 'yes'
        vars['route'] = 'finish'
    def select_write():
        if vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified' or vars.get('account_state') != 'ready' or vars.get('transfer_state') in ['pending', 'succeeded'] or notes:
            raise ValueError('Write prerequisites missing')
        attempts = structured(vars.get('promise_attempts', dict()), dict())
        agreed = [r for r in ledger if r['status'] == 'agreed']
        for row in agreed:
            date = datetime.date.fromisoformat(row['offer_date'])
            if row.get('confirmed') != 'yes' or not business(date) or date < today or row['offer_date'] > row['deadline'] or not row['floor'] <= row['offer_amount'] <= row['past_due'] or int(attempts.get(row['product_id'], 0)) >= 2:
                raise ValueError('Invalid confirmed promise')
        if agreed:
            row = agreed[0]
            vars['pending_promise'] = dict(product_id=row['product_id'], amount=row['offer_amount'], date=row['offer_date'])
            vars['route'] = 'save'
        else:
            vars['phase'] = 'finalize'
            finalize()
    def resolve_scope(value):
        s = str(value or '').strip().lower()
        if s == 'all':
            return [r for r in ledger if r['status'] not in ['recorded', 'paid', 'dispute', 'service_error', 'refused', 'hardship']]
        if s == 'current':
            return [r for r in ledger if r['product_id'] == vars.get('current_product')]
        ordinals = dict(first=0, second=1, third=2)
        m = re.fullmatch(r'(?:the )?(first|second|third)(?: product)?', s)
        if m:
            i = ordinals[m.group(1)]
            return [ledger[i]] if i < len(ledger) else []
        return [r for r in ledger if s and s in [str(r['product_id']).lower(), str(r.get('label', '')).lower()]]
    def remember_input(kind='proposal'):
        vars['pending_input'] = dict(event=kind, date_text=dt, amount_text=amount_text, product_scope=scope, amount_scope=amount_scope, proposal_items=items)
    if phase == 'hold' and vars.get('failed_operation') == 'verify' and event == 'answer':
        sub = structured(vars.get('security_submission', dict()), dict())
        phase = 'phone' if sub.get('field') == 'phone_last4' else 'dob'
        vars['phase'] = phase
        vars['security_buffer'] = ''
    result_phase = str(vars.get('phase_after_result', ''))
    vars['phase_after_result'] = ''
    if phase == 'load':
        if vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified':
            raise ValueError('Verification required')
        vars['route'] = 'lookup'
    elif phase == 'account_init':
        if vars.get('verification_state') != 'verified' or vars.get('account_state') != 'loaded':
            raise ValueError('Lookup prerequisites missing')
        products = structured(vars.get('products', []), [])
        if not products:
            products = structured(vars.get('lookup_response.data.products', []), [])
        if not products:
            indexed = dict()
            for key, value in list(vars.items()):
                match = re.fullmatch(r'lookup_response\.data\.products(?:\.(\d+)|\[(\d+)\])\.([a-zA-Z0-9_]+)', key)
                if match:
                    idx = int(match.group(1) or match.group(2))
                    indexed.setdefault(idx, dict())[match.group(3)] = value
            products = [indexed[i] for i in sorted(indexed)]
        if not 1 <= len(products) <= 3:
            raise ValueError('Invalid account product count')
        ledger = []
        seen = set()
        for p in products:
            pid = str(p.get('product_id', ''))
            kind = p.get('type')
            days = int(p.get('days_late', 0))
            full = number(p.get('past_due', ''))
            floor = number(p.get('minimum_payment', '') if kind == 'credit_card' else p.get('instalment_amount', ''))
            if not pid or pid in seen or not 1 <= days <= 45 or not 0 <= floor <= full:
                raise ValueError('Invalid account facts')
            if kind == 'credit_card':
                suffix = str(p.get('card_last4', ''))
                if not re.fullmatch(r'\d{4}', suffix):
                    raise ValueError('Missing card label')
                label = 'credit card ending ' + suffix
            elif kind in ['personal_loan', 'car_loan']:
                label = kind.replace('_', ' ')
            else:
                raise ValueError('Unknown product type')
            seen.add(pid)
            early = days <= 7
            ledger.append(dict(product_id=pid, label=label, past_due=full, days_late=days, floor=floor, band='early' if early else 'late', deadline=after_business(today, 12 if early else 7).isoformat(), budget=1 if early else 2, attempts=0, status='open', rejected=[], floor_offered='no', full_too_much='no', vague_count=0))
        vars['account_state'] = 'ready'
        vars['product_deadlines'] = dict((r['product_id'], r['deadline']) for r in ledger)
        vars['product_floors'] = dict((r['product_id'], r['floor']) for r in ledger)
        vars['product_bands'] = dict((r['product_id'], r['band']) for r in ledger)
        vars['account_facts'] = json.dumps(ledger)
        vars['phase'] = 'all'
        text = 'I am calling from the collections team about a late payment. ' + ' '.join('Your ' + r['label'] + ' has a past-due amount of ' + money(r['past_due']) + ' and is ' + str(r['days_late']) + ' days late.' for r in ledger)
        text += ' Can you make this payment today?' if len(ledger) == 1 else ' Can you pay all of them today?'
        collection_say(text)
    elif phase == 'finalize':
        finalize()
    elif phase == 'writing':
        select_write()
    elif phase == 'hold':
        operation = str(vars.get('failed_operation', ''))
        if event == 'human' and not notes:
            if vars.get('human_asked') == 'yes':
                request_transfer('general')
            else:
                vars['human_asked'] = 'yes'
                vars['identity_resume_phase'] = 'hold'
                vars['phase'] = 'identity_human'
                identity_say('May I try to help you first?')
        elif event == 'retry' and operation in ['verify', 'callback', 'lookup', 'transfer', 'note']:
            if operation == 'callback':
                sub = structured(vars.get('callback_submission', dict()), dict())
                d = datetime.date.fromisoformat(str(sub.get('date', '')))
                t = datetime.time.fromisoformat(str(sub.get('time', '')))
                if d not in [today, callback_next] or not datetime.time(10, 0) <= t <= datetime.time(19, 0) or datetime.datetime.combine(d, t) <= now:
                    vars['phase'] = 'callback'
                    identity_say('Please give another callback time. ' + vars['callback_facts'])
                else:
                    vars['route'] = 'callback'
